    {
      "id": "claim_f63b813198af4537bbc3d9a4d2709950",
      "statement": "The consentsGate condition composes: equals(@authenticated, 'true') so only signed-in callers are guarded, exclusions for path-prefix /auth and /token so blocked users can sign in and get tokens, an exclusion for the acceptance PATCH /users/{userId} with bson-request-whitelist(consents), and a final not (equals tos AND equals pp) clause that blocks when either acceptance is missing; /users/me is deliberately not excluded so the first session check trips the gate with no client probing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L135-L161",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:152607e653da37f5f18e11d56b3e53c87e63a611c2dfc3bc59005995c4e38be8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7604c6df719040dabbac22fd171a44ea",
      "statement": "The client signal module exports consentsBlocked as a readonly Vue ref, isBlocked/setBlocked to read and set it, and consentsOnError which calls setBlocked(true) on any 451 ApiError; consentsOnError is passed to createRhAuth as config.onError in main.ts, making it the only place that distinguishes 'blocked by consents' from 'signed out'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/consents-signal.ts#L18-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f647a57ed495d528a809cfe75998c039d5e24f6dae124a066bbf77ba11d07068:"
