      "statement": "ConsentsGate sits at the root of App.vue above RouterView because a blocked user has no session (/users/me is refused too), so authGuard would bounce them to login and they could never reach a screen to accept; the overlay is UX, not enforcement — removing it with dev tools leaves every request answered 451 by the server rule.",
