    {
      "id": "claim_19ae1f54db184ec6b8c910897cc9c407",
      "statement": "The userCanPatchOwnConsents permission exists because nothing authorizes PATCH /users/{userId} out of the box — without it the acceptance is a 403 and a guard never gets a say on an ACL-refused request; its predicate matches the caller's own id (@user._id or @user.sub), is restricted to the 'user' role and the consents whitelist, and its mongo mergeRequest stamps latestConsents with the derived versions and '@now' and $pushes the acceptance into the consents history, with latestConsents as a nested object since MongoDB refuses conflicting update operators on a field and a path inside it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L220-L249",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56499f2d0ad5eed28fb40c71ad06fe70a7a4e81e66811d8d67d473627ab1b050:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4a9f733df8ac441985b4b8a892fa861d",
      "statement": "The userConsentsSchema allows latestConsents (tos/pp strings required, acceptedAt as an escaped _$date BSON date) and consents as an array but requires none of them, because registration and invitation writes are validated at insert before consents or the team exist; requiring them would reject every registration and invitation. The schema step's check canonicalizes the stored schema so an older stored version counts as outstanding, and the collection binding is verified via /users/_meta because listing /users documents never reveals jsonSchema.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L204-L218",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3489aa0d533e0d0c0c8706b749aa63c0a0dc7b368ed88dc80dd90e416714f49:"
        },
        {
