          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d7de05259b55c9c2ddba192979f9b4b262c3d2ed3816c7183aa7b41ef1e88676:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_be76e69d00594c78b1f4cec4bd7a2c66",
      "statement": "The claims step PATCHes the service's auth-config 'account-properties-claims' to add latestConsents/tos and latestConsents/pp, merging with existing claims rather than replacing them; the guard reads the token, not the database, so a missing claim blocks every token-authenticated user forever. Only these two claims are added because the JWT payload is base64-readable and the consents history grows at every acceptance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L251-L278",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9d37d3e6a363b91d369e72b52f1ab716d1c3963465c87f873099c950c0eb02b0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_522aea889687400e9e3191fd49d1ff08",
      "statement": "The consentsGate guards rule is written with action 'block', status_code 451, on_error 'allow' (a rule that cannot be evaluated must not lock everyone out), and a message telling the user to accept the current documents; its check compares both the condition string and status_code, so bumping a version shows up as outstanding setup work rather than satisfied.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://ulabase.setup.consents.ts#L285-L320",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:61bb3204eef5b835755b0b6f6ddeb8cd77fc51636fd8e642903f24bd6671900f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c982dd3a3b304128b922dcffd817244b",
      "statement": "main.ts wires the gate into app bootstrap: consumeFragmentToken runs before createRhAuth so a token in the URL fragment is stored before the first session check, createRhAuth receives consentsOnError, and the global beforeEach runs the kit's authGuard/publicGuard on routes keyed by meta.guard, with routes without meta unguarded — so a blocked user's guard rejection is absorbed by the store and only consentsOnError reveals why.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main.ts#L36-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4865f6e002e7fa8ec5dd5d234b4c412353426ed775effc0f1a6bcec57c82a070:"
        },
        {
